 The approved `docs/product/plan.md` pipeline uses a small strict design brief and one validated geometry graph for vector drawing, proposed 3D and exact native binding.
 
+## Plan questions and design admission
+
+Plan discussions may finish without a geometry brief; actual design generation still requires the source-bound brief and scope checks before the engine runs.
+
+[[apps/domain-api/agent_workflow.py#interpret_brief_node]] preserves the brief and versioned answers without blocking general discussion. [[apps/domain-api/agent_workflow.py#dispatch_action]] asks unresolved geometry questions or records unsupported scope before generation. A narrow current-turn explicit refusal is honored, while unrecognized phrasing is not treated as a complete intent classifier. The recorded footprint-and-entry conditional is satisfied only by its matching current-run grouped receipt and rebuilt sources; other conditions are not inferred. `apps/domain-api/test_plan_general_admission.py` covers controlled graph routing, cancellation and versioned question resumption with mocked I/O.
+
 ## Output recovery
 
 Structured output, context, budget and step failures preserve usage and completed evidence while rejecting incomplete native operations. Continuation is an explicit user action.
